    [38;2;197;201;199m"Open" means I hadn't checked those things yet. I didn't exclude them on purpose. I wrote the spec down before finishing the grounding, so the product sentence promises things the spec can't[39m
    [38;2;197;201;199myet back.[39m

    [38;2;197;201;199mKimi's point holds. The "Done" test checks only that agents show up and can be stopped. It doesn't check:[39m

    [38;2;117;121;127m• [38;2;197;201;199mfollow[39m
    [38;2;117;121;127m• [38;2;197;201;199msteer[39m
    [38;2;117;121;127m• [38;2;197;201;199mkill[39m
    [38;2;117;121;127m• [38;2;197;201;199mthe transcript afterwards[39m
    [38;2;117;121;127m• [38;2;197;201;199msab-air[39m
    [38;2;117;121;127m• [38;2;197;201;199mmodel labels for non-Claude harnesses[39m
    [38;2;117;121;127m• [38;2;197;201;199mspend[39m

    [38;2;197;201;199mThose are all in the promise and all missing from the test, and the control part rests entirely on Herdr and Rex, which nobody has verified.[39m

    [38;2;197;201;199mKimi is checking the hook and control assumptions now, so I won't duplicate that. I'll fold its findings into [1mSPEC-fleet.md[0m[38;2;197;201;199m[48;2;47;48;54m when they come back.[39m

